  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The imaginary unit \\( i \\) extends the reals; complex numbers add, multiply, and have a modulus and conjugate.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Complex numbers",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( i^{2}=-1 \\); \\( z=a+bi \\) has modulus \\( |z|=\\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}} \\) and conjugate \\( \\bar{z}=a-bi \\), with \\( z\\bar{z}=|z|^{2} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Unit",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( i^{2}=-1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Form",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a+bi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Modulus",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Conjugate",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a-bi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\( |3+4i| \\).</p>\\[ \\sqrt{9+16}=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Modulus-argument form",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Write \\(z=-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,i\\) in modulus-argument form and find \\(z^4\\) using De Moivre's theorem.</p><p>\\(|z|=\\sqrt{1+3}=2\\). \\(\\arg z=\\pi-\\arctan\\sqrt{3}=\\pi-\\tfrac{\\pi}{3}=\\tfrac{2\\pi}{3}\\).</p><p>\\(z=2\\bigl(\\cos\\tfrac{2\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\tfrac{2\\pi}{3}\\bigr)\\). By De Moivre: \\(z^4=2^4\\bigl(\\cos\\tfrac{8\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\tfrac{8\\pi}{3}\\bigr)=16\\bigl(\\cos\\tfrac{2\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\tfrac{2\\pi}{3}\\bigr)=16(-\\tfrac{1}{2}+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}i)=-8+8\\sqrt3\\,i\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Given that \\(z_1=3+4i\\) and \\(z_2=1-2i\\), find \\(\\dfrac{z_1}{z_2}\\) in the form \\(a+bi\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Multiply by conjugate: \\(\\dfrac{(3+4i)(1+2i)}{(1-2i)(1+2i)}=\\dfrac{3+6i+4i-8}{1+4}=\\dfrac{-5+10i}{5}=-1+2i\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
